Hi,
I completely missed this PR and independently opened a [PR](https://github.com/podman-container-tools/podman/pull/29349) based on the `v1.44` changelog adding the `DnsNames` too, my bad.

Comparing it apart from much better tests, different approach how the `DnsNames` field in the compat endpoint gets populated and change in the `Aliases` semantics, I noticed three other differences that I wanted to discuss:
- I [used](https://github.com/simek-m/podman/blob/e4468b129a96d351e7e7d39e74b3c1c7b8254a59/libpod/networking_common.go#L718) `getNetworkPodName(c)` instead of `c.Name()`. Not sure what's more correct.
- I deduplicated the `DNSNames` based on the [Docker (Moby) implementation](https://github.com/moby/moby/blob/8430f1e347c785f5a2cd412e2f3e2fba55c33882/daemon/container_operations.go#L676). When I test that, it looks like this in this branch:
```json
{
  "Networks": {
    "podman": {
      ...
      "Aliases": [
        "844f6d6ce177"
      ],
      "DNSNames": [
        "dnstest",
        "844f6d6ce177",
        "844f6d6ce177"
      ]
    }
  }
```
- The [JIRA ticket ](https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/RUN-3314) also lists the libpod endpoint `GET /libpod/containers/json` to have `DNSNames` added (me adding that, also affected CLI).

Thanks.

> Oh maybe not then. I'll update the libpod endpoint. I don't think we need to worry about dedup?

Yeah, I think that with your other changes it's less of an issue. You can probably set multiple same aliases (haven't tried that), but it's a completely minor thing.

Edit:

Yes, you can, but it's on you if you set the same alias multiple times.
```json
{
  "Networks": {
    "podman": {
      ...
      "Aliases": [
        "alias",
        "alias"
      ],
      ...
      "DNSNames": [
        "dnstest",
        "alias",
        "alias",
        "19c1e70a47f0"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
